It depends on how important the conducts were for the game - if it's a
game which is all about playing foodless, or an illiterate atheist,
breaking the conduct can kill the game for me.
If i accidentally break 'minor' conducts like weaponless or find i'm
pretty much stuck unless i break wishless/genocideless/etc., i'll just
abandon the conduct rather than kill the character. In the first case
i may still stick to the conduct, even though it's no longer listed.

If i'm thoroughly disenchanted with a character, i'll usually just
walk her/him out of the dungeon. 

